Extension API: the save slots on the MAIN MENU's Load dialog too.

STATUS: NOT APPLIED. Written by work order 177, 26 September 2026, and
parked for Data's go/no-go (doc/briefs/177-parked-for-data.md). What was
shown, and only this: the patch applies to src/ext/ext_api.cpp at orion2re
orionlayer-local 2269749c (`patch -p1 --dry-run`), and the patched file
compiles with the engine's own flags from out/build/Linux/linux-debug/
build.ninja (g++ -std=gnu++20 -fsyntax-only, the cmake_pch.hxx include,
the ORION2RE_EXT define) — with a control: the same file with the new
constant misspelt is refused. It has not run.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_main_menu_save_slots.patch

then rebuild, and add its marker (`main_menu_load`) to
tools/version_check.py in the commit that records the apply.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    Open fix 14 (doc/ext_save_slots.patch, applied 16 September 2026)
    sends MSG_SAVE_SLOTS — each slot's status, type, name and stardate —
    while the GAME popup's Load or Save dialog is up, and only then:
    SerializeSaveSlots requires SCREEN_GAME. The MAIN MENU's LOAD GAME
    runs the same builder (Add_Game_Popup_Fields_ case 2,
    loadsave.cpp:223-266) through MAINMENU::Mainmenu_Load_Game_Popup_
    (mainmenu.cpp:187-189), which sets _screen_data 2 while
    _current_screen stays SCREEN_MAIN_MENU (10) — so a client sees the
    dialog's ten rows and knows nothing about what is in them. Reading
    SAVEn.GAM from a folder of its own is refused (OrionLayer
    fundament 60).

    With it, OrionLayer draws the main menu's Load dialog as it draws the
    GAME menu's; without it the dialog is shown as the game's own picture
    with the input passed through (work order 177's safety net).

One file, one condition. Nothing else moves.

--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -478,7 +478,15 @@
 static bool SerializeSaveSlots(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
                                int16_t current_screen) {
     buf.clear();
-    if (current_screen != SCREEN_GAME) {
+    // OrionLayer open fix 34: the MAIN MENU's Load dialog is the same
+    // builder (Add_Game_Popup_Fields_ case 2, loadsave.cpp:223-266) run
+    // by MAINMENU::Mainmenu_Load_Game_Popup_ (mainmenu.cpp:187-189), which
+    // sets _screen_data 2 while _current_screen stays SCREEN_MAIN_MENU —
+    // so its slots are sent too. Only the LOAD case: the main menu has no
+    // Save dialog.
+    const bool main_menu_load = current_screen == SCREEN_MAIN_MENU
+                                && MOX::_screen_data == 2;
+    if (current_screen != SCREEN_GAME && !main_menu_load) {
         return false;
     }
     const int16_t screen_data = MOX::_screen_data;
